  "title": "# merge-conflict-alerts Orchestrator build ID: merge-conflict-alerts (profile current, 5 steps).",
  "asked": "# merge-conflict-alerts Orchestrator build ID: merge-conflict-alerts (profile current, 5 steps). Use that record: follow its steps and models, tick steps as you finish, record session and cost on it. URGENT FIRST (step s1): fix PR #370 (branch claude/badges-notify-followup, badges + usage meter). GitHub refuses to merge it: 'Pull Request has merge conflicts'. Merge origin/main into the branch, resolve conflicts keeping both sides' intent, re-run the checks, push, and get it landed through the merge queue (Brett already approved its UI Review items). Report what conflicted. Then steps s2-s5: detect conflicts on every open PR; alert Brett with an approval (AmberX push AND console) with 'Fix conflicts now'; a persistent item on the fixed banner until resolved; approving launches an orchestrator conflict-fix job and re-queues the PR. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
